# Project Goal: Vietnam-Focused Nutrition App to Google Play

- Primary project objective: build a practical nutrition app that helps users track eating habits, health metrics, and personalized recommendations.
- Product decisions should prioritize user value, reliability, and readiness for production mobile release.
- Primary market focus: Vietnam users, with Vietnamese-first product thinking in UX/content/workflow proposals.
- Delivery target includes deployment to Google Play (CH Play), so implementation should consider:
  - stable user-facing flows (onboarding, tracking, recommendation, subscription),
  - robust error handling and analytics for production,
  - maintainable architecture and testability for release quality.
- Core target user segments to prioritize in planning and implementation:
  - users who do not know what to eat day-to-day,
  - users who want to improve and monitor personal nutrition,
  - gym/PT-oriented users who need goal-based meal and macro support.
- Feature and UX recommendations should be practical for Vietnam context:
  - local meal patterns and food naming,
  - budget-aware suggestions,
  - simple and fast daily logging experience.
- When proposing roadmap or features, prefer sequencing that accelerates Play Store launch readiness first, then advanced enhancements.
